{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-geometric","title":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-geometric","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":399,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-geometric","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-geometric","line":927,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[Bonnet--Myers diameter and compactness]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-geometric}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0267}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds, thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric}\n\n  Let $(M^n,g)$ be complete and connected, with $n\\ge2$. If\n  $\\sec\\ge k>0$, then $M$ is compact and\n  $\\operatorname{diam}(M,g)\\le\\pi/\\sqrt k$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  Tracing \\(\\sec\\ge k\\) over an orthonormal basis gives \\(\\operatorname{Ric}\\ge(n-1)k\\); apply \\cref{thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[Bonnet--Myers diameter and compactness] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a7065742d6368362d686f70662d72696e6f772d6d796572732d67656f6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0267</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23def%3Apet-ch6-sec-bounds\">↗ def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M^n,g)$\">$(M^n,g)$</span> be complete and connected, with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n\\ge 2$\">$n\\ge 2$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sec \\ge k&gt;0$\">$\\sec \\ge k&gt;0$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is compact and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {diam}(M,g)\\le \\pi /\\sqrt k$\">$\\operatorname {diam}(M,g)\\le \\pi /\\sqrt k$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Tracing <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sec \\ge k$\">$\\sec \\ge k$</span> over an orthonormal basis gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}\\ge (n-1)k$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}\\ge (n-1)k$</span>; apply <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d6d796572732d72696363692d67656f6d6574726963\">section 3</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_Sectio